    "rationale": "The project objective torch_communication.communication_kernel_sum_ms (baseline 94.49 ms, max-rank median of 93.52/94.49/110.06) is produced entirely by the 13 per-step NCCL AllReduce kernels dispatched through the two selected c10d::allreduce_ groups: 12 calls of 7,087,872 float32 elements (group f833b57a373d8262a384, call d0938de87369efd500322679) plus 1 call of 39,385,344 elements (group 8525af72c631b94e3dd0, call b8ade439d7b8bd5fb5c1029b), together exactly the 497,759,232-byte FP32 gradient payload (resources.json communication payload_coverage 13/13, unmatched kernels empty). Measured decomposition: the clean isolated calibration of the identical ops (collective_calibration-1af5837f) gives 3.565/3.649 ms per small bucket and 19.49/19.64 ms for the large one, a per-rank transport floor of about 62.3-63.5 ms that matches rank 1's in-step kernel sums (63.62-63.79 ms) and the nsys rank-0 sum (62.46 ms); rank 0's excess of ~31 ms is early-arrival waiting inside the first kernel (execution_timeline: seq21 duration 14.04 ms on rank 0 vs 3.62 ms on rank 1, all later kernels within ~90 us lockstep, union == sum so kernels are back-to-back on one stream), and both ranks finish the step at equal wall time (144.63/144.54 ms), proving the excess is idle spin rather than work. Because peer_access is 0 in both directions and NCCL runs over SHM/direct channels (resources.json transport/capabilities), the ~8 GB/s logical payload rate is a transport property and the dominant addressable term in the metric is the inter-rank arrival skew charged into kernel durations, plus per-op launch/protocol overheads (13 kernels). The skew direction flips between runs (nsys run: rank 1 sum 241 ms), so the fix must be symmetric. Both allreduce shapes belong to one logical gradient sync issued by the same DDP reducer, and any batching or launch-synchronization replacement must own every allreduce of the step to sequence its readiness exchange and group flushes; a single-group scope would interleave replaced and unreplaceable default allreduces on the same comm stream. The two groups are therefore one coherent joint boundary, and the affected calls are exactly the calls of both groups.",
    "hypothesis": "Replacing both allreduce dispatch sites jointly with a launch-synchronized, batched gradient allreduce will reduce the diagnostic max-rank NCCL kernel sum from ~94.5 ms toward the observed transport floor of ~63-66 ms (roughly 30%) while keeping step_ms within the 1.05x budget (<=151.86 ms vs baseline 144.6 ms). Mechanism: (1) each bucket request is queued and a lazy Work object is returned so the DDP reducer's async_op/wait semantics, ReduceOp SUM over contiguous FP32 bucket views (gradient_as_bucket_view=True) and the final-backward overlap structure are preserved, with flushes early enough that the currently small compute/comm overlap (8.8-21.1 ms) and the +7.2 ms step-time headroom are not consumed; (2) before the first NCCL launch of the step, the ranks exchange peer readiness through a mechanism that is not an NCCL kernel (for example the host-side shared-memory flag path NCCL itself uses, or an equivalent CPU-side handshake), so the early-arriving rank waits outside NCCL kernel durations instead of inside the first kernel - this is the hypothesized source of the ~31 ms rank-0 excess and, being symmetric, also covers the flipped-skew case observed under nsys; (3) the 13 requests are coalesced into fewer NCCL group launches (13 -> 1..few), removing per-op ring protocol startup/drain and launch overheads measured at roughly 0.1-0.4 ms per op. The per-byte transfer time is expected to stay ~8 GB/s (SHM/direct transport, no P2P), so no wire-time reduction is claimed. Test conditions and risks: gradient values must remain bitwise identical across ranks (ring element-wise summation order is expected to be preserved under grouped launches, but this must be validated against the atol=0.0/rtol=0.0 replica check and the reference gradient check), the readiness exchange must not itself launch NCCL kernels nor move gloo control-group barriers inside timing, and the benefit is a hypothesis to be confirmed by the framework's separately profiled objective samples, not by the perturbed discovery traces."
